# Project-owned build switches (nim.cfg is generated by nimby; keep it that way).
#
# -d:fast: the shipping/benchmark profile for the emulator. Measured on a
# Pi 3 (Cortex-A53): the runtime checks -d:release keeps on cost ~43 % of
# frame time; --mm:arc and -d:lto were noise. The referee build (make
# bench-check, tests) stays -d:release so a hidden out-of-range access
# still raises there.
when defined(fast):
  switch("define", "danger")
